<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa Ozz details cap share award.</title>
<headline>S.Africa Ozz details cap share award.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African investment holding firm Ozz Ltd said ordinary shareholders would be awarded 2.036 fully paid new ordinary shares for every 100 existing ordinary shares held in the company at close of business on July 11, 1997.</p>
<p>A company statement said the new shares would be issued at a price of 2,750 cents.</p>
<p>It said shareholders would be given the option to renounce their capitalisation share award for cash and would instead be paid 56.0 cents per existing ordinary share.</p>
<p>The new ordinary shares would be listed with effect from the start of trading on August 18, 1997.</p>
<p>--Johannesburg newsroom -27-11.482.1003</p>
